 ;
 ; Program for VOR/VOR, VOR-NDB, NDB-NDB navigation (aviation)
 ;
 ; DISCLAIMER:
 ; This program is designed for experimental navigation calculations over distances and at altitudes typical of general aviation (GA).
 ; It uses an approximate planar model of the Earth's surface, with corrections for the convergence of meridians towards the poles,
 ; rather than full spherical or ellipsoidal geometry.
 ; This approximation introduces systematic position errors that can become substantial over long distances.
 ; The magnitude of these errors depends on the geographical configuration and generally increases with distance.
 ; Consequently, the program is not suitable for the extended navigation distances typical of high-altitude airline operations.
 ; For educational and flight-simulation use only. Not suitable as a primary or safety-critical navigation aid in real aircraft.
 ;
 ; Operating conditions:
 ; The calculator must be in DEG mode, not RAD or GRAD (the initialization function E' ensures that).
 ; Southern latitudes and western longitudes must be negative.
 ; Magnetic declination is positive east and negative west.
 ; The aircraft's magnetic radials are measured FROM the VOR station, not the selected OBS course unless the CDI is centered with a FROM indication.
 ; Before using the program, press E' to initialize it to a well-defined state.
 ;
 ; VOR radials and NDB bearings can be treated identically as infinite, undirected lines.
 ; For an NDB, add the aircraft's magnetic heading to the relative ADF bearing, then add
 ; the local magnetic declination (also called magnetic variation), preferably at the aircraft's position.
 ; For a VOR, add the VOR's station declination to its magnetic radial.
 ; The 180-degree difference between an inbound NDB bearing and an outbound VOR radial is irrelevant
 ; to the intersection of infinite lines.
 ;
 ; Interface:
 ;
 ; A : input/output VOR/NDB 1 latitude               (DDDMM.mmmmm)
 ; B : input/output VOR/NDB 1 longitude              (DDDMM.mmmmm)
 ; C : input/output VOR 1/local magnetic declination (DDD.ddddddd)
 ; D : input VOR 1 magnetic radial/ADF 1 readout     (DDD.ddddddd)
 ;
 ; A': input/output VOR/NDB 2 latitude               (DDDMM.mmmmm)
 ; B': input/output VOR/NDB 2 longitude              (DDDMM.mmmmm)
 ; C': input/output VOR 2/local magnetic declination (DDD.ddddddd)
 ; D': input VOR 2 magnetic radial/ADF 2 readout     (DDD.ddddddd)
 ;
 ; SBR ( : store aircraft's magnetic heading in register 13 for calculation of absolute ADF bearing for NDB 1   (mnemonic: ( comes first)
 ; SBR ) : store aircraft's magnetic heading in register 14 for calculation of absolute ADF bearing for NDB 2   (mnemonic: ) comes second)
 ; SBR EE: store aircraft's magnetic heading in registers 13 + 14 for absolute ADF bearing for both NDB 1 and 2 (mnemonic: EE is double)
 ;
 ; SBR = : display the intersection angle in degrees (0-90) and the error margin amplification factor in test register t
 ; Call SBR = only AFTER calling E. This will work even after a rejection.
 ; Mnemonic: check whether the radials/bearings are (almost) parallel, and display a measure for the reliability of the position calculation
 ;
 ;
 ; E': erases registers 01-29, switches A' B' C' A B C to input (D and D' are always input) and sets DEG mode
 ;
 ; E : calculates latitude and longitude of the aircraft, switches A' B' C' A B C to output (D and D' are always input)
 ;
 ; However, BEWARE:
 ;
 ;                Error margin
 ; Intersection  amplification  Assessment
 ;    angle         factor
 ;
 ;   0 -5          >=11.47x       REJECT
 ;   5 -15        3.86-11.47x     Poor
 ;  15 -30        2.00-3.86x      Marginal
 ;  30 -60        1.15-2.00x      Good
 ;  60 -90        1.00-1.15x      Excellent
 ;
 ; In case of rejection, a blinking "9.9999999 99" is displayed and execution is stopped (and register t is set to zero).
 ;
 ; Output:
 ; x (current display) = result aircraft's latitude              (DDDMM.mmmmm)
 ; t (test register)   = result aircraft's longitude             (DDDMM.mmmmm)
 ; Register 07         = result aircraft's latitude              (DDD.ddddddd)
 ; Register 08         = result aircraft's longitude             (DDD.ddddddd)
 ; Register 11         = VOR/NDB 1 true radial/true absolute ADF (DDD.ddddddd)
 ; Register 12         = VOR/NDB 2 true radial/true absolute ADF (DDD.ddddddd)
 ; Register 16         = rejection factor, reject if < sin(5)
 ; Register 17         = intersection angle
 ; Register 18         = error margin amplification factor
 ;
 ; Conversion functions DDDMM.mmmmm <=> DDD.ddddddd:
 ; SBR  .  = DDDMM.mmmmm => DDD.ddddddd (to decimal format)
 ; SBR +/- = DDD.ddddddd => DDDMM.mmmmm (to cockpit format)
 ; Output: current display and register 00

 ; Registers:
 ; 00 Contains the conversion result DDDMM.mmmmm <=> DDD.ddddddd from SBR . and SBR +/-
 ; 01 VOR/NDB 1 latitude                              (DDDMM.mmmmm)
 ; 02 VOR/NDB 1 longitude                             (DDDMM.mmmmm)
 ; 03 VOR 1/local declination                         (DDD.ddddddd)
 ; 04 VOR/NDB 2 latitude                              (DDDMM.mmmmm)
 ; 05 VOR/NDB 2 longitude                             (DDDMM.mmmmm)
 ; 06 VOR 2/local declination                         (DDD.ddddddd)
 ; 07 Result aircraft's latitude                      (DDD.ddddddd)
 ; 08 Result aircraft's longitude                     (DDD.ddddddd)
 ; 09 VOR/NDB 1 magnetic radial/relative magnetic ADF (DDD.ddddddd)
 ; 10 VOR/NDB 2 magnetic radial/relative magnetic ADF (DDD.ddddddd)
 ; 11 VOR/NDB 1 true radial/true absolute ADF         (DDD.ddddddd) (mnemonic: 11 = 1)
 ; 12 VOR/NDB 2 true radial/true absolute ADF         (DDD.ddddddd) (mnemonic: 12 = 2)
 ; 13 NDB 1 magnetic aircraft heading at readout ADF  (DDD.ddddddd)
 ; 14 NDB 2 magnetic aircraft heading at readout ADF  (DDD.ddddddd)
 ; (these can be the same if the ADF readouts are made in rapid succession or if the aircraft's magnetic heading is stable)
 ; 15 Signed denominator = sin(RCL11-RCL12)
 ; 16 Rejection factor = abs(sin(RCL11-RCL12)), reject if < sin(5)
 ; 17 Intersection angle
 ; 18 Error margin amplification factor
 ; 19 VOR 2 lat.  - VOR 1 lat.  (Y2 - Y1)
 ; 20 VOR 2 long. - VOR 1 long. (X2 - X1) * COS( mean latitude )
 ; 21 Signed distance d1 from VOR 1 (first in degrees, eventually in nm)
 ; 22 Signed distance d2 from VOR 2 (first in degrees, eventually in nm)
 ; 23 Result aircraft's latitude  based on VOR 2      (DDD.ddddddd)
 ; 24 Result aircraft's longitude based on VOR 2      (DDD.ddddddd)
 ; 25 VOR/NDB 1 latitude                              (DDD.ddddddd)
 ; 26 VOR/NDB 1 longitude                             (DDD.ddddddd)
 ; 27 VOR/NDB 2 latitude                              (DDD.ddddddd)
 ; 28 VOR/NDB 2 longitude                             (DDD.ddddddd)
 ; 29 COS( mean latitude of VOR 1 and VOR 2 )
 ; 30 Scratchpad for conversions

